// Title: Office Application Startup - Office Test
// Sigma ID: 3d27f6dd-1c74-4687-b4fa-ca849d128d1c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: omkar72
// Date: 2020-10-25 | Modified: 2023-11-08
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1137.002
// Description: Detects the addition of office test registry that allows a user to specify an arbitrary DLL that
//   will be executed every time an Office application is started
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/unit42-technical-walkthrough-office-test-persistence-method-used-in-recent-sofacy-attacks/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_office_test_regadd.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Software\\Microsoft\\Office test\\Special\\Perf"
